  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Siderite is a mineral composed of iron (II) carbonate&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.&nbsp;It is a widespread mineral that is an ore of iron.&nbsp;</p><p>Calamine:&nbsp;Zinc ore is most commonly found as zinc carbonate&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ZnCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> known as calamine or smithsonite.&nbsp;</p><p>Malachite <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CuCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>Cu</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></math>,&nbsp;&nbsp;Malachite&nbsp;is a copper carbonate hydroxide mineral</p><p>Cryolite&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>AlF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>, which consists of Aluminium, Sodium &amp; Fluorine.</p>",
